                          "gap": 16,
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "id": "NSqBo",
                              "name": "aiTitle",
                              "fill": "$--foreground",
                              "content": "AI in Healthcare: Current Impact and Future Promise",
                              "fontFamily": "Geist",
                              "fontSize": 16,
                              "fontWeight": "600"
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "id": "qKgAK",
                              "name": "aiP1",
                              "fill": "$--foreground",
                              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                              "width": "fill_container",
                              "content": "Artificial intelligence is rapidly transforming healthcare delivery and outcomes across multiple domains. In diagnostics, deep learning models now match or exceed radiologist accuracy in detecting conditions like diabetic retinopathy, lung cancer nodules, and breast cancer from medical imaging [1][2]. Google Health's AI system demonstrated 94.5% sensitivity in mammography screening, reducing false positives by 5.7% compared to human readers [3].",
                              "lineHeight": 1.65,
                              "fontFamily": "Geist",
                              "fontSize": "$--font-size-sm",
                              "fontWeight": "normal"
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "id": "h9Vmu",
                              "name": "aiP2",
                              "fill": "$--foreground",
                              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                              "width": "fill_container",
                              "content": "In drug discovery, AI has compressed the traditional 10-15 year development timeline significantly. Insilico Medicine's AI-discovered drug reached Phase II clinical trials in just 30 months from target identification [4]. Meanwhile, AlphaFold's protein structure predictions have been used by over 2 million researchers, accelerating understanding of disease mechanisms [5][6].",
                              "lineHeight": 1.65,
                              "fontFamily": "Geist",
                              "fontSize": "$--font-size-sm",
                              "fontWeight": "normal"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
